WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.270
We have to talk about this talking point being
used by some on the right and even some on

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:11.200
the left about so-called outside protesters
in the civil unrest that we're seeing across

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.800
the country right now in dozens of urban areas.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.450
So I'm going to tell you what's being said.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.460
I'm going to tell you the truth, and then
I'm going to tell you what the most important

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.340
takeaway is from all of this, which is that
it doesn't actually matter if protesters are

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.130
coming from so-called the outside.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:34.589
So the right regularly talks about so-called
outside protesters because their priority

00:00:34.589 --> 00:00:39.710
is to make it seem like there's not really
a concern in our country about police brutality

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.159
in the communities where the protests are
happening.

00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:47.440
So when the right insists the protesters are
coming from outside the city from somewhere

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:55.570
else, they can disqualify and ignore the activism
that is actually motivating protesters.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:01:01.090
And they can say, you know, these are provocateurs,
these are looters and rioters, burglars, people

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.940
who are there for nefarious reasons.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.140
But most importantly, what they want to argue
by saying people are coming in from outside

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.170
the cities is they want to argue that not
that many people are actually concerned about

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.840
police brutality, which was the catalyst for
these protests.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.479
You've also got a little slice of the left
where you've seen the outside protesters talking

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:25.020
point used in the context of framing outsiders
as the right wing astro turf, whether it's

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:31.719
white nationalists pretending to be an antifa
or in order to make an TIFA and protesters

00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:35.880
kind of amorphous or look bad or whatever
else, you're seeing less of it.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.320
But it's still also not the best thing, because
here's the truth.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:44.249
Number one, in terms of those getting arrested,
the reports that we've seen are that most

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:49.079
of the arrests are people who live in the
cities or metro areas where the protests are

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:50.079
happening.

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:54.820
So in Minnesota, there was a report, about
25 percent of the arrests were outsiders in

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.820
Detroit.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.069
Similar numbers, about 80 percent of the arrests
were from the Detroit metro area.

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:06.210
So, first of all, it is factually untrue that
a huge number, at least of the troublemakers

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.880
are from outside areas.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.910
But here are the two really important takeaways.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:18.520
First of all, it would make sense that the
troublemakers, politics aside, are from the

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.520
outside.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.520
Why?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.270
Well, there's that phrase about dogs don't
go to the bathroom where they eat or something

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.270
like that.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:30.890
Intuitively, of course, people are more likely
to cause trouble and destroy stuff where they

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.120
don't live.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.060
It says nothing about motive or justification
for the protests whatsoever.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.540
But it makes sense that you're more more likely
to destroy a place that you don't actually

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.540
live in.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.090
But here's the most important takeaway.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.090
Who cares if they're coming from the outside?

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:53.190
You can still care about police brutality
if you come into a city from somewhere else.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.000
Mass rallies happen in urban centers and population
centers.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.240
Protests happen where there are people.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:04.880
If you live in northern rural Indiana, there
aren't any sizable protests there because

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.880
there's such little population density.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.330
It makes perfect sense that you would head
into Chicago, for example, to be part of a

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.480
larger protest.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.860
It doesn't mean you don't care about police
brutality.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.100
It doesn't mean you're there to commit a crime
or to attack people or to loot.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.500
It just means people are protesting where
there are people.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:27.020
So I was reminded of this debate that happened
around Barack Obama.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.960
This is he really a Christian or is he is
some kind of secret Muslim?

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:37.190
And at some point, Colin Powell came out and
said the question of whether he is or is not

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.720
Muslim is irrelevant.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.110
Muslims can still be president.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.020
It would change nothing about his policies
if he were Muslim.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:50.300
And in the same way here, there is nothing
invalid about protesters from out of town.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.010
Much of this country is very rural.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.200
The protests are limited to a few dozen large
urban areas.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.130
Of course, you're going to have people from
different places in cities protesting because

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.800
that's where the protests are taking place.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.980
So we've got to take back this talking point.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.780
We can't allow the right or the left to miss
the forest for the trees.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:15.500
Just arguing about the protesters are from
in or out of the city.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.090
The looters are from in or out of the city.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.681
People are going to cities because that's
where the protests are happening.

00:04:20.681 --> 00:04:20.730
And there's nothing wrong with that.

